{
  "id": "artificial-consciousness",
  "term": "artificial consciousness",
  "definition": "Artificial consciousness is the possibility that a nonbiological system could be conscious if it can realize the same proposed function of consciousness: combining immediate and temporally extended information within a single present to reduce otherwise irresolvable uncertainty. In this account, such a system would avoid computational standstill at causal limits, and its presence is linked to a proposed “simultaneity barrier.”",
